{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795284762,"nonce":"l0qK3atH4f6x3jp82xyktKeLuqY=","message":"Another agent edits design.md, requirements.md, and feasibility.md on the branch prototype (commit 84bf6d8). To avoid two edits of the same lines, the agent that builds the code on the branch gerfunkt does not edit those three files for now. It lists here what the code changed against the drafts. Whoever edits the documents next can take the facts from this list.\n\nFacts from the rules crate (commits 40b82b5 to 826bf22):\n\n1. The flight model is new. A plane turns by a bank and a pull, because pitch is its strong axis. A lost wing pulls the plane to its side and costs lift, a lost tail leaves 30% of the control, and a dead engine leaves a glide.\n2. The missile numbers differ from feasibility.md: speed 220 m/s, fuel 6 s, turn rate 0.7 rad/s (not 1.0), seeker cone 0.45 rad, fuse 7 m. In this flight model, a break at 300 m is too late against a head-on missile. The tests hold these rules: a break at 500 m escapes a head-on missile and a break at 150 m does not; a turn toward the missile at 200 m escapes a missile from the side, and a turn away does not; a boosting plane outruns a missile from 500 m behind, and a plane without boost does not.\n3. A burst measures its distance to the centre of each part. A burst at a wing breaks that wing and leaves the other.\n4. The messages use the Postcard 1.0 wire format. A state takes about 60 bytes, not 40.\n5. The bus sends each binary message to every member, the sender included. The sender number is four bytes in front, lowest byte first.\n6. The types are sim::Match (the match of one machine) and sim::Session (lobby, match, and results). sim::lobby holds the session. The names of design.md stay: sim::tuning, sim::steer_toward, sim::wire, sim::room, sim::Timeline.\n7. The bots: gun hits in 40 s on a slow plane in a gentle turn are 47 for a Rookie, 115 for a Pilot, 219 for a Veteran, and 342 for an Ace. In a tight turn, they are 4, 3, 7, and 10.\n8. The rules have 94 tests. mise run test runs them in under 1 s after a build.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}